.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="A catalyst lowers a reaction&#x27;s activation energy without changing its thermodynamics, which -- via the Arrhenius equation (chemistrykit.kinetics.systems.arrhenius) -- can speed the reaction up by many orders of magnitude even for a modest reduction in E_a. compare_catalyzed_rate quantifies this, and turnover_frequency/ turnover_number are the standard measures of catalytic activity and durability.">

